  (label "USB_OTG0_DP"
    (at 196.85 73.66 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "a4ec4638-7273-5be2-a9e5-ce7542ba0ee7")
  )
  (text "ENGINEERING DESIGN NOTES (USB-C Daughterboard):\n1. Active VBUS OVP/OCP Protection & Power-Tree Coordination (U2, TPS259470ARPWR): 28.3 mOhm back-to-back FET eFuse between VBUS_IN (J1)\n   and VBUS (J2) routed with wide stitched F.Cu/B.Cu copper pours. Precision 1% divider R6 (34.8k) + R7 (5.62k) + R8 (9.09k)\n   sets UVLO = 4.04V typ rising and OVLO = 6.54V typ rising (6.32V min..6.75V max) / 5.94V typ falling (5.77V min > 5.50V vSafe5V max).\n   R9 (1.37k 1% on ILM) sets active OCP = 2.43A typ (2.19A min..2.68A max < 3.0A 6-pin J2 contact rating), while the system power budget\n   (2.4W typ / 6.0W peak = 1.20A @ 5V) and mainboard BQ25895 charger input limit (capped <= 2.00A via R8=200R 1.78A typ / 1.95A max hardware ILIM\n   and <= 2.00A software IINLIM ceiling) stay strictly below U2 I_OL(min) = 2.19A. C5 (4.7 nF on DVDT Pin 7) sets dV/dt = 5.11 V/ms,\n   while C4 (1 uF 25V) and Schottky diode D5 (PMEG3005EL_315) on VBUS decouple local output transients and clamp negative inductive kickback.\n2. 22V Standoff Flat-Clamp VBUS_IN Surge TVS (D3, ESTVS2200DRVR C42400188): V_RWM = 22.0V, V_BR = 25.8V (> 20V USB-PD and > 6.75V U2 OVLO)\n   and flat clamping V_CL = 27.6V typ / 28.6V max at 70A 8/20us (< 28.8V U2 abs max), allowing U2 to open-circuit sustained 6.5V-20V DC\n   overvoltages without D3 conducting DC current. Unswitched VBUS_IN capacitance C1 (1 uF 50V) + C3 (1 uF 50V via 0.33W 2.2R R3) = 2.0 uF (<= 2.2 uF).\n3. Biased & Isolated USB 2.0 ESD Clamp (U1, USBLC6-2P6): U1 Pin 5 (USB_ESD_VBUS, decoupled by 100 nF 50V C2 to GND) is biased from protected VBUS\n   via 1 kOhm R10 (USB_ESD_BIAS) and 70V ultra-low-leakage blocking diode D4 (BAS70L_315) at ~4.7V DC.\n4. Compensated 5.075 kOhm Effective CC1/CC2 Rd Termination: R1 and R2 are 6.8 kOhm 1% (0402WGF6801TCE C25917) on USB_CC1_CONN / USB_CC2_CONN\n   in parallel with 10 kOhm series isolation resistors R4/R5 + 10 kOhm mainboard SARADC shunt resistors R49/R50, yielding\n   Rd(eff) = 6.8 kOhm || (10 kOhm + 10 kOhm) = 5.075 kOhm (-0.5% from 5.10 kOhm nominal, well within USB Type-C 5.1 kOhm +/- 10%)."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
